    "q-347278": {
      "dom_id": "step-q347278",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "A tutoring center offers private lesson packages. When the price of a package is $$40,$ the center books all $80$ available sessions. For every $$4$ increase in the package price, one fewer session is booked. If the cost of providing each session is $$16,$ what price should the center charge to maximize its profit?\n\nTo maximize profit, the center should charge $$$\n{{field-1}}\nper session.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we apply the candidates test.\n\nLet $x$ represent the number of unbooked sessions. Then the number of **booked** sessions is $(80-x),$ and the **price per session** is $(40+4x).$\n\nSo, the total revenue is\n\n$$\nR(x)=(80-x)(40+4x).\n$$\n\nExpanding, we get\n\n$$\nR(x)=-4{x}^{2}+280x+3200.\n$$\n\nThe cost of providing each booked session is $$16,$ so the total cost is\n\n$$\nC(x)=16(80-x)=1280-16x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the profit function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =R(x)-C(x) \\\\  & =(-4{x}^{2}+280x+3200)-(1280-16x) \\\\  & =-4{x}^{2}+296x+1920.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given the domain $0\\le x\\le 80.$\n\nTo find the maximum, we take the derivative:\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(x)=-8x+296.\n$$\n\nSolving ${P}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get:\n\n$$\nx=37.\n$$\n\nSince ${P}^{″}(x)=-8<0,$ this point is a maximum. Since $P(x)$ is quadratic, this maximum is global.\n\nNow, if $x=37$ sessions are unbooked, then the price is:\n\n$$\n40+4(37)=188.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to maximize profit, the center should charge $$\\,\\,188$ per session.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
